# Kubernetes & GitOps Rules — suparship

## Installation Profiles

### Profile Definitions

| Profile | Components | Use Case |
|---------|------------|----------|
| `demo` | k3d + ArgoCD + Kargo + sample app + ingress | Local development, demos |
| `core` | ArgoCD + Kargo + ingress controller | Minimal GitOps platform |
| `full` | core + metrics + logging + additional tools | Feature-complete install |

### MVP Scope Rules

- `demo` and `core` profiles MUST NOT require paid services
- `demo` MUST work offline after initial image pull
- Heavy addons (Prometheus stack, ELK, Istio) MUST be `full` profile only
- Each profile MUST complete install in < 5 minutes on reasonable hardware

### Component Matrix

```yaml
# internal/profiles/profiles.yaml
profiles:
  demo:
    cluster: k3d
    components:
      - argocd
      - kargo
      - traefik        # ingress
      - sample-app
  core:
    components:
      - argocd
      - kargo
      - traefik
  full:
    extends: core
    components:
      - prometheus
      - grafana
      - loki
```

## ArgoCD Conventions

### Application Naming

```
{service}-{environment}
```

Examples:
- `api-dev`
- `frontend-staging`
- `api-pr-123` (previews)

### Required Labels

```yaml
metadata:
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: suparship
    suparship.io/environment: dev
    suparship.io/service: api
    suparship.io/project: myproject
```

### Required Annotations

```yaml
metadata:
  annotations:
    suparship.io/generator-version: v0.1.0
    suparship.io/source-template: service-v1
    argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "10"  # When ordering needed
```

### Namespace Conventions

| Namespace | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `argocd` | ArgoCD system |
| `kargo` | Kargo system |
| `suparship-system` | suparship controllers/jobs |
| `env-{name}` | Environment workloads (e.g., `env-dev`, `env-staging`) |
| `preview-{name}` | Preview environments (e.g., `preview-pr-123`) |

### Application Spec Standards

```yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: api-dev
  namespace: argocd
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: suparship
    suparship.io/environment: dev
    suparship.io/service: api
  finalizers:
    - resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io
spec:
  project: default  # Or project-specific
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/org/repo
    targetRevision: HEAD
    path: environments/dev/services/api
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: env-dev
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
      - CreateNamespace=true
```

## Kargo Conventions

### Stage Naming

```
{environment}
```

Simple names matching environment: `dev`, `staging`, `prod`

### Promotion Pipeline

```yaml
apiVersion: kargo.akuity.io/v1alpha1
kind: Stage
metadata:
  name: dev
  namespace: kargo-project
spec:
  subscriptions:
    repos:
      images:
        - repoURL: ghcr.io/org/app
          semverConstraint: ">=1.0.0"
  promotionMechanisms:
    gitRepoUpdates:
      - repoURL: https://github.com/org/gitops
        writeBranch: main
        kustomize:
          images:
            - image: ghcr.io/org/app
---
apiVersion: kargo.akuity.io/v1alpha1
kind: Stage
metadata:
  name: staging
spec:
  subscriptions:
    upstreamStages:
      - name: dev
  # ... promotion config
```

### Freight Naming

Kargo auto-generates freight names. Do not override.

## Ingress Host Conventions

### URL Patterns

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Service in env | `{service}.{env}.localhost` | `api.dev.localhost` |
| Preview | `{preview-name}.preview.localhost` | `pr-123.preview.localhost` |
| ArgoCD | `argocd.localhost` | `argocd.localhost` |
| Kargo | `kargo.localhost` | `kargo.localhost` |

### Ingress Generation

```yaml
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: api-dev
  namespace: env-dev
  annotations:
    traefik.ingress.kubernetes.io/router.entrypoints: websecure
    traefik.ingress.kubernetes.io/router.tls: "true"
spec:
  rules:
    - host: api.dev.localhost
      http:
        paths:
          - path: /
            pathType: Prefix
            backend:
              service:
                name: api
                port:
                  number: 80
  tls:
    - hosts:
        - api.dev.localhost
```

### Preview Name Sanitization

Preview names MUST be DNS-safe:

```go
func SanitizePreviewName(input string) string {
    // pr-123 -> pr-123 (unchanged)
    // feature/my-thing -> feature-my-thing
    // PR_123 -> pr-123
    name := strings.ToLower(input)
    name = regexp.MustCompile(`[^a-z0-9-]`).ReplaceAllString(name, "-")
    name = regexp.MustCompile(`-+`).ReplaceAllString(name, "-")
    name = strings.Trim(name, "-")
    if len(name) > 53 {
        name = name[:53]
    }
    return name
}
```

## Template Rendering

### Helm-First Strategy

- Primary rendering: Helm charts with values injection
- Overlays: Kustomize for environment-specific patches
- Raw manifests: Only for simple static resources

### Template Input Format

```yaml
# service.yaml (input to renderer)
apiVersion: suparship.io/v1
kind: ServiceTemplate
metadata:
  name: api
spec:
  template: service-v1       # Reference to templates/service-v1/
  values:
    image: ghcr.io/org/api
    replicas: 2
    env:
      LOG_LEVEL: info
      DATABASE_URL: ref:db-secret.url  # Secret reference
```

### Rendering Rules

1. Load template from `templates/{name}/`
2. Merge values from service.yaml + environment defaults
3. Execute Helm template
4. Apply Kustomize overlays if present
5. Sort output by kind/namespace/name
6. Write to output directory

### Output Location

```
gitops-output/
├── environments/
│   ├── dev/
│   │   └── services/
│   │       └── api/
│   │           ├── deployment.yaml
│   │           ├── service.yaml
│   │           └── ingress.yaml
│   └── staging/
└── previews/
    └── pr-123/
        └── api/
```

### Commit Generated Output

- Generated output SHOULD be committed to Git
- ArgoCD syncs from committed output (not from renderer)
- Enables GitOps audit trail and easy diff review
- CI can generate and commit, or local `suparship render --commit`

## Namespace Isolation

### Environment Isolation

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: env-dev
  labels:
    suparship.io/type: environment
    suparship.io/environment: dev
```

### Preview Isolation

Previews MUST be in isolated namespaces:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: preview-pr-123
  labels:
    suparship.io/type: preview
    suparship.io/preview: pr-123
  annotations:
    suparship.io/ttl: "7d"  # Auto-cleanup hint
```

### Network Policy (Future)

MVP does not enforce network policies. Production SHOULD add:
- Deny all ingress by default
- Allow only from ingress controller
- Allow intra-namespace traffic

## Resource Ordering

When generating multi-resource manifests, sort by:

1. Namespaces
2. CRDs (if any)
3. ConfigMaps, Secrets (references)
4. Services
5. Deployments/StatefulSets
6. Ingresses
7. ArgoCD Applications

Use sync-waves in ArgoCD for deployment ordering:

```yaml
annotations:
  argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "0"   # Namespace
  argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "10"  # ConfigMaps
  argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "20"  # Deployments
  argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "30"  # Ingress
```
